    fix(734): preconfig level reaches the no-roles boot model; never send a zero-budget thinking block

    Rework of the ai-teammate review round 1:

    - BLOCKING: the FA_PROVIDER_* thinkingLevel only reached a Model via the
      roles chain pin. A boot with no roles: section (or a keyless preconfig
      that cannot pin a chain) printed the level in the notice while the
      booted fallback/default model carried none. buildCliDefaultModel gains
      a thinkingLevel parameter and _buildModel/both bin call sites forward
      faPreconfig.thinkingLevel - the notice claim is now always true.
    - E2: a ceiling at/below the answer floor clamped the ladder budget to 0
      and still sent thinking {type: enabled, budget_tokens: 0} - an invalid
      request. _addThinkingParam now omits the thinking block when the
      effective budget is 0; max_tokens still goes out at the clamped
      ceiling. (The adapter has no per-request note channel - pure-Dart lib;
      the note half of E2 stays the boot-time notice.)
    - SUGGESTION: the E1 note compares against the anthropicMessagesApi const
      instead of a hardcoded 'anthropic-messages' and is reworded to 'not
      wired to the config-carried thinkingLevel' - accurate for both
      no-thinking adapters (openai-completions) and thinking-capable-but-
      unwired ones (google).

    Tests: buildCliDefaultModel level threading (no-roles path) + absent
    stays null; tiny-ceiling payload omits thinking and keeps max_tokens at
    the ceiling. Full targeted suites (providers, model_roles, preconfig,
    parity) green; headless FA_TEST_STREAM_SCRIPT smoke re-verified both
    notice lines.

